# See kernel/logger/Kconfig: the ANDROID symbol is gone in 6.12, so the
# fragments opt in explicitly.
config ANDROID_LOW_MEMORY_KILLER
	tristate "Android lowmemorykiller"
	default n
	help
	  This is the Android lowmemorykiller driver. It monitors memory usage
	  and kills processes when memory is low, based on their oom_adj scores.
	  This driver was removed from mainline Linux in 6.12 but is still
	  required for Android 4.x and earlier (Android 5.0+ uses userspace lmkd).

	  If you are building Android 4.x or earlier, say Y.